(Hello World: a power ballad in which no letter is ever written down.)
(Rockstar counts the letters of each word in a poetic literal, one digit)
(per word, so "burning up" is 7 then 2, which is 72, which is the code)
(for a capital H. Cast turns that number into the character it stands)
(for, and "with" glues the characters together.)
(There is not one string literal in this song. Not one letter.)
(Rockstar v2. Everything in brackets is a comment, which is why Rockstar)
(has no parentheses in its expressions.)

My heart is burning up                             (7 2     -> 72  -> H)
My echo is a loneliness everlasting                (1 10 11 -> 101 -> e)
My longing is a melancholy farewell                (1 10 8  -> 108 -> l)
My ocean is heartbroken, unbreakable, everlasting  (11 11 11 -> 111 -> o)
My pause is cold fire                              (4 4     -> 44  -> comma)
My silence is why me                               (3 2     -> 32  -> space)
My wonder is farewell tonight                      (8 7     -> 87  -> W)
My rage is a heartbroken fire                      (1 11 4  -> 114 -> r)
My dream is a melancholy wilderness                (1 10 10 -> 100 -> d)
My finale is the end                               (3 3     -> 33  -> bang)

Cast my heart
Cast my echo
Cast my longing
Cast my ocean
Cast my pause
Cast my silence
Cast my wonder
Cast my rage
Cast my dream
Cast my finale

Let the song be my heart with my echo with my longing with my longing
Let the song be the song with my ocean with my pause with my silence
Let the song be the song with my wonder with my ocean with my rage
Let the song be the song with my longing with my dream with my finale

Shout the song
